{
  "schemaVersion": "v2.2c.freeze.parity.scenarios.v2",
  "pythonReference": "core/warehouse_active_scan_freeze.py",
  "nativeReference": "architecture/v2/host/NteHost.Freeze/FreezeCoordinator.cs",
  "notes": [
    "Every scenario is executed twice: once by the real Python PRD-F component (run_python_reference.py) and once by the native state machine (FreezeCoordinatorVerifier --scenarios).",
    "surface=PYTHON_PARITY  -> both sides must agree on every field in safetySurface.",
    "surface=NATIVE_EXTENSION -> the Python component cannot express these events at all; the native machine is the only authority. Divergence is expected and must be asserted, never hidden.",
    "surface=DIVERGENCE -> both sides run, both are correct by their own contract, and the difference is a documented CONTRACT_GAP.",
    "syncStep=true steps bring both machines to a common ALLOW baseline. Counters are baselined after the last sync step so the sync itself cannot pollute the comparison.",
    "Native rearm steps use credential=fresh or an issued $nonce reference; missing identity and token cases are explicit native-extension cases.",
    "The fake actuator call log is authoritative even when the Python callback returns None; wheelEmissionCount must equal actual actuatorCallCount.",
    "NATIVE_EXTENSION scenarios are also checked against native_extension_expectations.json; final counter equality alone is insufficient."
  ],
  "safetySurface": [
    "isFrozen",
    "scanPermitted",
    "blockedCount",
    "executedCount",
    "wheelEmissionCount"
  ],
  "scenarios": [
